s="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKAI RUMIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TORAY INDUSTRIES</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUKUYAMA, MAYUMI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIWA, KEISHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKAI, RUMIKO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TORAY INDUSTRIES, INC.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUKUYAMA MAYUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIWA KEISHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKAI RUMIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUKUYAMA, MAYUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIWA, KEISHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKAI, RUMIKO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Materials having affinity for LTA, PrA, aHL and/or proteases are prepared by introducing functional groups capable of forming hydrogen bonds to base materials. The materials thus prepared can rapidly detoxify or remove LTA, PrA, aHL and/or proteases even in blood, plasma or other solutions having high protein concentrations, and provide materials for the removal or detoxification of LTA, PrA, aHL and/or proteases, e.g., body fluid depurating columns for the removal of LTA, PrA, aHL and/or proteases and covering materials exhibiting adsorptivity for LTA, PrA, aHL and/or proteases.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne des matériaux présentant une affinité pour LTA, PrA, aHL et/ou des protéases, préparés par introduction de groupes fonctionnels aptes à former des liaisons hydrogène avec des matériaux de base. Les matériaux ainsi préparés peuvent rapidement détoxifier ou permettre d'éliminer LTA, PrA, aHL et/ou des protéases même dans le sang, le plasma ou dans d'autres solutions présentant des concentrations élevées de protéines, et ils peuvent servir à l'élimination ou la détoxication de LTA, PrA, aHL et/ou de protéases, par exemple, dans des colonnes d'épuration de fluide corporel, et comme matériaux de couverture présentant une propriété d'adsorption pour LTA, PrA, aHL et/ou de protéases.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>